      "strategyName": "Primal Groudon Recycle",
      "weather": "Extreme",
      "adventureEffect": "None",
      "difficulty": "2★",
      "text": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>Mega Raichu Y is an excellent addition to Electric themed battle parties with its ability to DPS in small windows and potential power in Zap Cannon+. Due to its very fragile and mostly non-threatening movesets this solo is quite simple.</p><h4>Est Time to Win: 170.5s - 210.5s</h4><h2>Main Strategy</h2><p>Utilizing Primal Groudon, comfortably DPS Mega Raichu per cycle until Primal Groudon requires healing. Be mindful to <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-clean-exit\" target=\"_blank\">exit the fight </a>without having leftover energy as this would lower DPS significantly if repeated too often.</p><p><br></p><p>Mega Raichu Y has 1 counter point to Primal Groudon in learning Surf. As a result if it learns Surf, it is recommended to add additional ground attackers. Lots of damage &amp; energy will be absorbed from surf so it is wise to not over extend using each attacker. A recommended strategy is <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-hot-swap\" target=\"_blank\">swapping</a> to the next attacker when below 25-30% health. </p><p><br></p>",
